    excerpt: "The shift to hybrid and remote work has moved ergonomic risk from a controlled office environment to thousands of unmonitored home setups — kitchen tables, lounge chairs, and improvised workstations. Addressing WFH ergonomics is now both a WHS obligation and a workforce health priority.",
